<p>Wes Streeting, who resigned as Britain’s health secretary last week, said on May 16 that he would stand in any Labour leadership contest to replace Prime Minister Keir Starmer, telling a Progress conference in London that Labour needed “a proper contest”. Streeting became the first Labour MP to say publicly that he would bid for the party leadership. Because Labour remains in government, the winner would be expected to become prime minister. He has not formally triggered a contest and said any race should wait until Greater Manchester Mayor Andy Burnham can try to return to Parliament. Streeting used the appearance to call Brexit a “catastrophic mistake,” advocate a “new special relationship” with the European Union and say Britain should one day rejoin the bloc. That position differs from Starmer’s approach: Starmer opposed leaving the EU but, as prime minister, has rejected seeking re-entry or making major concessions on issues such as immigration. Starmer has rejected calls to step down after Labour suffered heavy local election losses, and Labour rules require any challenger to secure support from at least 20% of the party’s MPs before triggering a leadership election.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/HY7KfkIIp2TVZ4vuTITOLlCHB58kZSKrDTb27X4CBxC9NTB4VYQGimFYZWWE4z_66icG_N_Bj3gPZYq5gs6vVi8jbSIOIsTpIKmQF9C9JpelUgmhq_6gHOVDfaTLBSOD2DKIbrRUkA1Vb-eX5uacdiJV8_IPZNHFqip0ARw5JSFr-k6L2nS-ilVStvK1zFNRVl3GvaGZvrGFmJfYiJtLzhhdSKHhmPBHqdfMnzAYEdmQIG1wuOEjjN_byw7534bZUkccVp2xIyaJzDBsZ1jkfXVK_38O' alt='Wes Streeting speaking at the Progress Conference at Convene in London' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Streeting profile: Streeting, 43, is described as coming from a working-class background and the right flank of Labour, with pro-market and anti-Brexit positions.</li><li>Resignation reason: In his resignation letter, Streeting said he had “lost confidence” in Starmer’s leadership and argued that Starmer lacked vision and direction.</li><li>Fiscal pledge: Burnham committed to Rachel Reeves’ fiscal rules in an effort to reduce market jitters as he prepared for a possible leadership challenge.</li><li>Makerfield test: Burnham is seeking Labour selection for the Makerfield by-election, a Brexit-voting constituency where Reform UK pressure has made EU policy politically sensitive.</li><li>Internal response: Streeting’s allies defended his decision to reopen the EU issue after criticism from within Labour.</li></ul><blockquote>We need a new special relationship with the EU, because Britain’s future lies with Europe – and one day back in the European Union. - Wes Streeting</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Andy Burnham: Burnham said he saw a long-term case for rejoining the EU but was not advocating that position in the Makerfield by-election, saying Britain should focus on domestic issues affecting people now. (<a href='https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/entry/streeting-throws-down-brexit-gauntlet-to-burnham-as-labour-splits-erupt_uk_6a096647e4b0ee71697307a1'>HuffPost UK</a>)</li><li>Kevin Hollinrake: The Conservative Party chairman said Labour was “relitigating Brexit” instead of governing and called the leadership dispute a distraction from the cost of living, the economy, public services and defence. (<a href='https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/entry/streeting-throws-down-brexit-gauntlet-to-burnham-as-labour-splits-erupt_uk_6a096647e4b0ee71697307a1'>HuffPost UK</a>)</li><li>Liberal Democrats: Liberal Democrat leader Ed Davey said Streeting would need to offer more than Starmer’s existing EU “red lines” if he wanted to succeed him. (<a href='https://www.huffingtonpost.co.uk/entry/streeting-throws-down-brexit-gauntlet-to-burnham-as-labour-splits-erupt_uk_6a096647e4b0ee71697307a1'>HuffPost UK</a>)</li><li>Steven Fielding: The University of Nottingham politics expert said Streeting has “a very acute political sense and an ability to communicate,” but that questions remain about how his politics fit the Labour Party. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/2000862/right-leaning-streeting-set-to-mount-challenge-for-labour-leadership'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/6338ad6f-cf26-44c6-96e4-c64f1db615dd'>Burnham plays down rejoining EU after Streeting advocates Brexit reversal</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/2000862/right-leaning-streeting-set-to-mount-challenge-for-labour-leadership'>Right-leaning Streeting set to mount challenge for Labour leadership</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/official-wes-streeting-labour-party-britains-prime-minister-133045646'>It&#x27;s official: Wes Streeting of the Labour Party wants to be Britain&#x27;s next prime minister</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/may/17/culture-secretary-lisa-nandy-says-wes-streeting-rejoin-eu-call-odd'>Top of Labour in row over EU as Nandy challenges Streeting’s remarks</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330459098/wes-streeting-right-leaning-labour-politician-set-to-run-for-leadership'>Wes Streeting: Right-leaning Labour politician set to run for leadership</a> - aaj.tv</li><li><a href='https://www.walesonline.co.uk/news/wales-news/wes-streeting-says-leaving-eu-33960591'>Wes Streeting says leaving EU was a &#x27;catastrophic mistake&#x27;</a> - walesonline.co.uk</li><li><a href='https://www.thenational.scot/news/26114352.labour-party-feud-wes-streeting-calls-uk-rejoin-eu/'>Labour Party feud after Wes Streeting calls for UK to rejoin EU</a> - thenational.scot</li><li><a href='https://www.lavanguardia.com/internacional/20260516/11539999/exministro-britanico-sanidad-dice-presentara-contienda-liderazgo-laborista.html'>El exministro Wes Streeting dice que se presentará a la contienda por el liderazgo laborista</a> - lavanguardia.com</li><li><a href='https://www.irishnews.com/news/uk/streeting-makes-call-to-rejoin-the-eu-as-starmers-rivals-gather-pace-YGZEQ6